{"id":"h241","run":2,"role":"test_right","category":"science-chemistry","question":"What is the theoretical density for calcium, since it crystallizes in the face-centered cubic unit cell, where a = 3.48°A, z = content = 3.\nIs the correct answer \"5.238 × 10^3 kg/m^3\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"With the given inputs (a=3.48 Å, z=3, M=40.08), the density is about 4.74×10³ kg/m³.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The proposed value 5.238×10³ kg/m³ does not follow from the given data.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Reproducing 5.238×10³ kg/m³ with these inputs would require z≈3.3, which matches neither 3 nor 4.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Using the standard FCC z=4 gives about 6.3×10³ kg/m³, which also does not match the proposed value.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Rounding or atomic mass differences cannot explain the gap between the computed and proposed values.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-0.7,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The problem's inputs are internally inconsistent because FCC has 4 atoms per cell, so z=3 contradicts the structure.","confidence":0.85,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The real lattice parameter of calcium is about 5.58 Å, not 3.48 Å.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The inconsistencies do not change the arithmetic but mean the intended 'correct' answer depends on which inputs are intended.","confidence":0.6,"lean":0.2,"theta":0.9425,"phi":3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":-0.3,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"suppor